    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0234" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg200"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that Mr. Uhl’s
                    dispatch No. 372, of the 3d instant, reporting that he had made further
                    intervention on behalf of Mr. Alfred Meyer, has been received.</p>
                <p>The Department fully approves Mr. Uhl’s course in regard to the matter, and would
                    be glad to have you keep this case in mind in view of the importance of the
                    principle involved.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
